+
+#pragma once
+
+#include <CryMath/Cry_Color.h>
+
+//! Decision 08 - the plate's diffuse as the terrain's macro colour, LIVE and non destructive.
+//!
+//! Where this sits. The engine's runtime macro colour is a pooled atlas whose editor half is a PULL:
+//! CTerrainNode::SetupTexturing sees a node marked eTES_SectorIsModified_AtlasIsDirty and calls
+//! CTerrainNode::UpdateNodeTextureFromEditorData (terrain_node.cpp:117-142, :528-583), which builds the
+//! tile row by row out of C3DEngine::m_pEditorHeightmap->GetColorAtPosition and DXT compresses it into
+//! the atlas slot. That callback IS CHeightmap. So the overlay is applied to the row buffer CHeightmap
+//! hands back (Heightmap.cpp, GetColorAtPosition) - the OUTGOING buffer only. CRGBLayer, the level's
+//! actual colour, is never written: CRGBLayer::Serialize flushes every dirty tile to disk on every level
+//! save (RGBLayer.cpp:1088), so anything written there would silently become permanent at Ctrl+S
+//! (research 13 section B / section 3).
+//!
+//! Consequences that fall out of that choice, all of them wanted:
+//!  * nothing to restore. The atlas is a cache; its truth is CRGBLayer. Untick, move or delete a plate
+//!    and the same pull repaints the tile from the untouched source. There is no baseline array and no
+//!    restore bug class (research 13 section 1.3-1.4).
+//!  * it survives streaming for free: CTerrainSectorTexture's StreamOnComplete re-arms the dirty flag
+//!    (terrain_sector_tex.cpp:170-173), so the next pull re-applies the overlay.
+//!  * EDITOR ONLY, by nature. The game loads terraintexture.pak, which is produced from CRGBLayer by
+//!    CGameExporter::ExportSurfaceTexture (GameExporter.cpp:1068-1070). Nothing written into the atlas
+//!    can reach it. Shipping the colour is what terrain.commit_plate_colour (Commit Colour) is for, and
+//!    the two tiers share BlendPlateColourIntoTexel and ITerrainPlateCommit::GetCommitWeightAtWorld, so
+//!    "Commit Colour" means literally "make what you are looking at permanent".
+namespace TerrainPlateColourOverlay
+{
+
+//! THE blend, shared by the live overlay and by terrain.commit_plate_colour. Both sides to linear, lerp
+//! there, back to gamma - the terrain painter's own recipe (ImagePainter.cpp:310-335); blending gamma
+//! values directly makes the rim band read too dark.
+//!
+//! destination and the return value are one terrain colour texel in the RGB layer's packed layout,
+//! blue | green << 8 | red << 16 (RGBLayer.h:63), which is also the layout CHeightmap::GetColorAtPosition
+//! hands to the engine. source is the plate's albedo when bUseAlbedo is set, otherwise the flat tint;
+//! tint multiplies the albedo when bUseAlbedo is set (and IS the source when it is not).
+uint32 BlendPlateColourIntoTexel(uint32 destination, ColorB source, ColorB tint, bool bUseAlbedo, float weight);
+
+//! Once per editor frame. Re-enumerates the plates whose Terrain Colour From Plate is on, and marks the
+//! terrain texture sectors under a plate that appeared, moved, changed or went away, so that the engine
+//! pull repaints them. Debounced: a plate that reports itself settling (a drag in progress) is left
+//! alone until it settles, and no plate repaints more often than kRepaintFrameInterval.
+void Update();
+
+//! True when at least one plate is currently asking for the overlay. Cheap; the stock path must stay
+//! byte identical when this is false.
+bool IsActive();
+
+//! Composites the live plates over one row of terrain colour texels, in place. Called from
+//! CHeightmap::GetColorAtPosition with the row it is about to return.
+//!
+//! The engine asks for a row along WORLD Y at a fixed world X (terrain_node.cpp:562 passes m_nOriginY
+//! first and m_nOriginX second, and CHeightmap's first argument is the fpx of the RGB layer, which is
+//! the world Y - research 12 sections 1.2 and 3.1). worldStepY is the node's own texel size in metres,
+//! so ancestor tiles automatically get a wider filter footprint and the rim antialiases at every level.
+void ApplyToRow(uint32* pRow, int count, float worldYStart, float worldStepY, float worldX, float rgbTexelSizeMeters);
+
+}
